{"meta":{"createDate":0,"tags":[],"id":"block-definition-fr","title":"RTO · objectif de reprise"},"blocks":{"id":"block-definition-fr","flavour":"myoxus:page","props":{"title":{"$virgultum:internal:text$":true,"delta":[{"insert":"RTO · objectif de reprise"}]}},"children":[{"id":"block-definition-fr-surface","flavour":"myoxus:surface","props":{"elements":{}},"children":[],"type":"block"},{"id":"block-definition-fr-note","flavour":"myoxus:note","props":{"displayMode":"both","index":"a0","xywh":"[0,0,870,100]"},"children":[{"id":"block-definition-fr-1","flavour":"myoxus:callout","props":{"text":{"$virgultum:internal:text$":true,"delta":[{"insert":"RTO · Recovery Time Objective","attributes":{"bold":true}},{"insert":"\nDurée maximale acceptable entre l’interruption d’un service et son rétablissement. Le RTO est un objectif fixé, et non une durée moyenne d’indisponibilité mesurée.\nDistinction : le RPO décrit la perte de données maximale acceptable comme la durée écoulée depuis le dernier point de reprise."}]},"appearance":"accent","backgroundColorName":"blue","icon":{"type":"emoji","unicode":"ℹ️"},"textProtection":"source"},"children":[],"type":"block"}],"type":"block"}],"type":"block"},"type":"page"}